  "details": "We have Selfie Expression, and it adjusts the head's position/rotation. Can we get a toggle under Camera Tracking/Selfie Expression that allows it to control your camera/view?\n\nA good example of this is TrackIR and LookPilot, so when you rotate your real head, and it's tracked, your game view adjusts from the first person of your avatar.\n\nThis can create a half-VR/pseudo-VR experience for desktop users, and means you no longer really need to move your view with your mouse unless you're doing major adjustments.\n\nThis also allows for HeadChop components to work as expected in desktop mode while in VR and reduce clipping for non-humanoid avatars, eg. taur rigs, and furry avatars that have a first-person snout that you otherwise can't use with Selfie Expression on.\n\nIt should be its own toggle, as it's best with a high framerate camera, though lower framerates can be smoothed.",
